   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(169,166,157)\">So I have tried to use library clv in R, so I create the code: </p><p style=\"font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(169,166,157)\"><br></p><p style=\"font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(169,166,157)\">engine.eval(&quot;library(clv)&quot;);</p><p style=\"font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(169,166,157)\"><br></p><p style=\"font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(169,166,157)\">However, when I run the code, it report exception that <span style=\"color:rgb(186,203,186)\">Exception in thread &quot;main&quot; </span><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;color:rgb(4,51,255)\">org.renjin.eval.EvalException</span><span style=\"color:rgb(186,203,186)\">: Could not load package org.renjin.cran:clv.</span></p><p style=\"font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(169,166,157)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(186,203,186)\"><br></span></p><p style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(186,203,186);font-family:Monaco;font-size:11px\">I would like to know, what&#39;s the proper way to use library in </span><font color=\"#bacbba\" face=\"Monaco\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">renjin??</span></font></p></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "R4XsL4hAAgAJ",
   "from": "Bertram, Alexander",
   "author": "f06db63329fab1f9",
   "date": "2015-12-07T07:54:09Z",
   "subject": "Re: How to use a library in renjin",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<p dir=\"ltr\">Hi there,<br>\r\nIf you are embedding Renjin in a Java application, then the library&#39;s jar needs to be on the classpath.</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">You can find documentation on this here:<br>\r\n<a href=\"http://docs.renjin.org/en/latest/introduction.html#using-cran-packages-in-renjin\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.renjin.org/en/latest/introduction.html%23using-cran-packages-in-renjin&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793343828680000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1E1VT-oWgiLuIE-RjGWr1z\">http://docs.renjin.org/en/latest/introduction.html#using-cran-packages-in-renjin</a></p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Please note that it looks like the clv package is not completely compatible, check <a href=\"http://packages.renjin.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://packages.renjin.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793343828680000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0-3Q8Kzo72mm_IaKuP4Y-j\">packages.renjin.org</a> for details.</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Alex</p>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(169,166,157)\">So I have tried to use library clv in R, so I create the code: </p><p style=\"font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(169,166,157)\"><br></p><p style=\"font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(169,166,157)\">engine.eval(&quot;library(clv)&quot;);</p><p style=\"font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(169,166,157)\"><br></p><p style=\"font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(169,166,157)\">However, when I run the code, it report exception that <span style=\"color:rgb(186,203,186)\">Exception in thread &quot;main&quot; </span><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;color:rgb(4,51,255)\">org.renjin.eval.EvalException</span><span style=\"color:rgb(186,203,186)\">: Could not load package org.renjin.cran:clv.</span></p><p style=\"font-size:11px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(169,166,157)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(186,203,186)\"><br></span></p><p style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(186,203,186);font-family:Monaco;font-size:11px\">I would like to know, what&#39;s the proper way to use library in </span><font color=\"#bacbba\" face=\"Monaco\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">renjin??</span></font></p></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></div>"
    ],
